  "sourceFacts": {
    "title": "Both loaded orange leads visibly descend across the FRONT opening from above the straight upper lip into separate openings in the cavity floor. They are not merely lines concealed behind the board.",
    "DualP1": "Two orange spans enter the open front recess; the loose exterior rope/knot is visible. The near lip occludes the exact floor intersections, so this supports the front-side visible approach but not the complete hidden connection.",
    "DualP2": "The board without rope shows two daylight openings through the recess floor. This corroborates independent floor-to-back holes; no connecting rear U channel is shown."
  },
